KNOWNBUG
contract.solast
--sol contract.sol --contract C --unwind 35 --no-unwinding-assertions --no-standard-checks
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
Asserts `keccak256(abi.encodeWithSignature(...)) == keccak256(abi.encodeCall(...))`
for equivalent selectors, but our identity-abi model returns nondet
BytesDynamic for `returns (bytes memory)` functions whose body is an
identity-chain uint256.  Two such calls produce distinct nondet
values, so the equality cannot be proved.  Previously reported
SUCCESSFUL only because the bytes_static_from_uint pack loop was
truncated at low unwind, leaving the high bytes zero on both sides
and silently making memcmp match.  Fixing the pack to straight-line
32 assignments exposed the over-approximation — revisit when the
abi model distinguishes signatures/selectors semantically.
